# Agent Infrastructure Enforcement

When you change **1+ files** under `.cursor/` (rules, skills, hooks, agents, references), run the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill before reporting done. Write a stamp to `.cursor/hooks/state/agent-validation-stamp.md`.

## Layer 1: This Rule (L2g — Advisory)

Tells you to validate. Fires when glob-matched `.cursor/` files are edited.

Skip **only** for changes limited to `.cursor/hooks/state/` (runtime artifacts like stamps and hashes).

## Layer 2: Stop Hook — Hint (L5 — Enforced)

`post-task-check.sh` Check 6 verifies `agent-validation-stamp.md` exists and is fresh (< 10 min). If missing, it sends a `followup_message` once per unique set of changed files.

## How to Validate

Follow the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill checklist manually. Write a stamp to `.cursor/hooks/state/agent-validation-stamp.md`.

## Triggered Rule Notice

When this rule applies, mention it early:
"This touches .cursor/ infrastructure — agent-infrastructure validation will be required."
